E["npc:altsoba-ragetotem"] = {t="npc",n="Altsoba Ragetotem",z="felwood",s="At Bloodvenom Post, Altsoba Ragetotem equips Horde travelers for the blighted woods of Felwood. The tauren weaponsmith offers maces, staves, and axes.",h="At Bloodvenom Post, Altsoba Ragetotem equips Horde travelers for the blighted woods of Felwood.",sec={{t="Armorer of Bloodvenom Post",b="Altsoba Ragetotem outfits Horde scouts and travelers bound for Felwood’s corrupted woods from Bloodvenom Post. The outpost stands in the forest’s heart, amid demonic corruption and tainted wildlife. Keeping supplies moving there is a grim necessity. Altsoba offers sturdy crescent axes and heavy war mauls, so warriors entering the corrupted timberlands have weapons at hand.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Altsoba Ragetotem?",a="Altsoba Ragetotem is a tauren vendor at Bloodvenom Post, the Horde encampment in Felwood. He provides basic heavy weapons to travelers and defenders braving the blighted valley.",al={"who is altsoba","altsoba ragetotem","tauren at bloodvenom post"}},{q="What does Altsoba sell?",a="Altsoba sells standard melee weapons, including battle staves, morning stars, war mauls, and axes. They offer dependable steel to those venturing deep into Felwood.",al={"altsoba wares","altsoba vendor items","what weapons does altsoba sell"}},{q="Where can I find Altsoba Ragetotem?",a="Altsoba Ragetotem can be found at Bloodvenom Post, along the cliffs overlooking Felwood’s foul waters and tainted glades.",al={"altsoba location","where is altsoba","bloodvenom post vendor location"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde operative, you can rely on Altsoba for martial supplies while holding your ground in one of Kalimdor’s most corrupted regions.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you share Altsoba’s Ragetotem heritage and the steadfastness his people bring to a land suffering under demonic blight."},kw={"altsoba","bloodvenom post","felwood","ragetotem","tauren","vendor","weaponsmith"},rel={"subzone:bloodvenom-post","zone:felwood","topic:tauren"},src={"Altsoba Ragetotem"}}
E["npc:greta-mosshoof"] = {t="npc",n="Greta Mosshoof",z="felwood",s="At the Emerald Sanctuary, Greta Mosshoof works to stop the corruption spreading through Felwood. She stands with the Emerald Circle and other guardians of nature, studying the taint and sending scouts into Jaedenar.",h="At the Emerald Sanctuary, Greta Mosshoof works to stop the corruption spreading through Felwood.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Forest",b="At Felwood’s southern edge, Greta Mosshoof works from the Emerald Sanctuary with the Emerald Circle. Corruption is consuming the ancient woods. Greta and her allies seek to understand the spreading rot and push it back. Her investigations follow Felwood’s poisoned waters and the foul cultists hidden within Jaedenar.",sp=0},{t="Striking at the Shadow Council",b="Greta Mosshoof directs efforts against the Shadow Council in Jaedenar. Its corrupted springs and foul wards feed the sickness choking Felwood. She sends travelers to sample the tainted waters and seek help from Islen Waterseer on the distant coast. They must also destroy the ritual braziers that shield the demonic cabal from intrusion.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Greta Mosshoof?",a="Greta Mosshoof works with the Emerald Circle at the Emerald Sanctuary in Felwood. She aids travelers and druids investigating and undoing the demonic blight poisoning the forest.",al={"greta mosshoof lore","who is greta mosshoof","greta felwood"}},{q="What faction does Greta Mosshoof belong to?",a="Greta Mosshoof belongs to the Emerald Circle, a neutral organization devoted to healing nature. She guides both Alliance and Horde adventurers.",al={"is greta mosshoof horde or alliance","greta mosshoof reputation","greta faction"}},{q="Why is Greta sending adventurers into Jaedenar?",a="Jaedenar is the Shadow Council’s stronghold in Felwood. The council pumps demonic bile into the waterways and maintains wards that shelter demons. Greta sends travelers to break its rituals and purify the blighted springs.",al={"why jaedenar quest","greta mosshoof jaedenar","forces of jaedenar reason"}},{q="What is Greta Mosshoof's connection to Islen Waterseer?",a="Greta Mosshoof is friends with Islen Waterseer, a wise shaman who lives along the coast of the Barrens. After Greta finds corrupt water samples from Felwood, she sends travelers to seek Islen’s spiritual mastery and purify the fluid. Then it can cleanse the poisoned springs.",al={"greta and islen","islen waterseer connection"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see how the Cenarion Circle sets faction ties aside to restore Kalimdor’s wilderness and heal the scars of the Burning Legion.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you see Greta’s devotion to healing the Earth Mother’s wounds, even far north in lands once guarded solely by the night elves."},kw={"corrupt water","emerald circle","emerald sanctuary","felwood","greta mosshoof","islen waterseer","jaedenar"},rel={"subzone:emerald-sanctuary","zone:felwood","subzone:jaedenar","npc:islen-waterseer","topic:tauren"},src={"Greta Mosshoof"}}
E["npc:winna-hazzard"] = {t="npc",n="Winna Hazzard",z="felwood",s="At Bloodvenom Post, Winna Hazzard studies the blight spreading through Felwood's living things. The Forsaken researcher watches local wildlife and experiments on corrupted creatures, often laughing beside her feline companion.",h="At Bloodvenom Post, Winna Hazzard studies the blight spreading through Felwood's living things.",sec={{t="A Peculiar Researcher",b="At Bloodvenom Post, Winna Hazzard studies Felwood's unnatural decay. The Forsaken researcher watches local wildlife and tests tainted water and venomous samples. Her jovial, manic manner can mask callous motives. With liquids drawn from the land, she corrupts the small kitten at her side.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Winna Hazzard?",a="Winna Hazzard studies Felwood's corruption at Bloodvenom Post in north-central Felwood. She asks travelers to gather samples from the wilderness.",al={"winna hazzard","who is winna","felwood cat lady"}},{q="What happens to her kitten?",a="When travelers bring Winna a filled flasket of corrupted liquid from the surrounding woods, she feeds it to her kitten. The liquid twists the creature into a Corrupted Cat, and Winna laughs maniacally.",al={"winna kitten","corrupted cat","felwood cat experiment"},sp=1},{q="What is Winna Hazzard's goal in Felwood?",a="Winna seeks to understand and harness biological blights. She studies how Felwood's widespread corruption alters living beasts, as many Forsaken apothecaries and scholars do.",al={"winna hazzard motive","why is winna in felwood"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="As Forsaken, Winna pursues corruption with dark eccentricity, reckless curiosity, and little regard for natural harmony.",["faction:Horde"]="At Bloodvenom Post, Winna asks passing Horde travelers to gather corrupted reagents for her strange research."},kw={"bloodvenom post","felwood","forsaken","kitten","winna hazzard"},rel={"subzone:bloodvenom-post","zone:felwood","topic:forsaken","npc:altsoba-ragetotem"},src={"Winna Hazzard"}}
E["npc:xavathras"] = {t="npc",n="Xavathras",z="felwood",s="Among the ruins at Constellas, Xavathras directs the Jadefire satyrs' work. He serves Xavaric and corrupts an ancient moonwell in Felwood.",h="Among the ruins at Constellas, Xavathras directs the Jadefire satyrs' work.",sec={{t="Corruptor of Constellas",b="At the Ruins of Constellas in Felwood, Xavathras commands the Jadefire satyrs. Their tents stand among old elven stonework, beside a moonwell he seeks to defile for Xavaric, another satyr. Xavathras poisons its pure waters with demonic energy, deepening the corruption gripping the forest. Night elves such as Eridan Bluewind seek his death, for his work threatens any effort to restore the woodland.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Xavathras?",a="At the Ruins of Constellas in Felwood, Xavathras commands the Jadefire satyrs. He serves Xavaric and works to corrupt the ancient elven moonwell among the ruins.",al={"who is xavathras","xavathras lore","who is the satyr boss constellas"}},{q="Where can Xavathras be found?",a="Xavathras camps among the satyr tents at the Ruins of Constellas, an ancient night elf site in southern-central Felwood.",al={"xavathras location","where is xavathras","ruins of constellas satyr"}},{q="Why does Eridan Bluewind want Xavathras dead?",a="Eridan Bluewind wants Xavathras dead because he is corrupting a moonwell and worsening Felwood's demonic defilement. Eridan seeks to defend the forest and halt its corruption.",al={"why kill xavathras"}},{q="Who is Xavathras working for?",a="Xavathras works for Xavaric, another satyr in Felwood who seeks to further the Legion's lingering grasp on the corrupted forest.",al={"who is xavathras master","xavaric xavathras"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see in Xavathras what became of ancient kin turned demonic beasts. He also desecrates sacred moonwells.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you know Xavathras's poisoning of pure waters affronts nature and threatens Felwood. His work must be stopped."},kw={"constellas","felwood","jadefire","moonwell","satyr","xavaric","xavathras"},rel={"subzone:ruins-of-constellas","zone:felwood","topic:satyr","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale","quest:6921"},src={"Xavathras"}}
E["subzone:bloodvenom-falls"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodvenom Falls",z="felwood",s="Toxic water pours over Felwood’s northern cliffs at Bloodvenom Falls. It feeds the Bloodvenom River, carrying demon-spawned rot down the mountains and beyond.",h="Toxic water pours over Felwood’s northern cliffs at Bloodvenom Falls.",sec={{t="A Fountain of Rot",b="Bloodvenom Falls pours over the bluffs in Felwood, a vivid wound in Kalimdor’s ancient forests. Once pristine, the water was warped by demonic magic and the Burning Legion’s remnants during the Third War. The falls feed the Bloodvenom River, which winds through the heart of Felwood. Then the tainted torrent rushes down the mountain slopes and becomes the foul Wildbend River in Darkshore, carrying blight beyond Felwood’s borders.",sp=0},{t="Ecological Poison",b="Runoff from Bloodvenom Falls stains the riverbed and warps all it touches. Twisted treants, sickening beasts, and aggressive slimes breed along the swampy banks around its spray. To druids and wardens trying to contain Felwood’s rot, the falls show how deeply northern Kalimdor’s waters remain sickened at their source.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does the water from Bloodvenom Falls flow?",a="The falls feed the Bloodvenom River, which winds across Felwood. It then cascades down the mountains into Darkshore and becomes the corrupted Wildbend River.",al={"where does bloodvenom river go","bloodvenom falls river path","where does it drain"}},{q="Why is the waterfall corrupted?",a="During the Third War, the Burning Legion’s demonic magic saturated the region and corrupted Felwood’s wild forests. Fel blight entered the springs and high mountain streams that feed the falls, turning their water into toxic muck.",al={"why is bloodvenom falls green","why is the water poisoned","what corrupted bloodvenom falls"}},{q="Does the corruption at the falls affect other zones?",a="Yes. The waters plunge from Felwood down the western mountain crests into Darkshore. There they emerge as the contaminated Wildbend River and carry rot toward the coast.",al={"does felwood poison darkshore","how does it affect darkshore","darkshore river pollution"}},{q="Can the waters of Bloodvenom Falls be purified?",a="The Cenarion Circle keeps seeking ways to cleanse Felwood, but the river holds a vast volume of deeply saturated demonic taint. Curing the falls remains a monumental struggle, and the corruption is unresolved.",al={"can druids fix bloodvenom falls","is bloodvenom falls cleansable","cleaning the waterfall"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see Bloodvenom Falls as a bitter sight for the Cenarion Circle. Its waters carry Felwood’s vile sickness into the lands below.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Bloodvenom Falls feeding the poisoned Wildbend River in Darkshore. Its waters threaten ancestral homes and coastal sanctuaries."},kw={"bloodvenom falls","bloodvenom river","corruption","darkshore","felwood","slime","waterfall","wildbend river"},rel={"subzone:bloodvenom-river","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:felwood","zone:darkshore"},src={"Bloodvenom Falls"}}
E["subzone:bloodvenom-post"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodvenom Post",z="felwood",s="At Bloodvenom Post, Horde guards watch Felwood’s high cliffs above Darkshore. Their tauren-style settlement stands amid demonic taint and corrupted wildlife.",h="At Bloodvenom Post, Horde guards watch Felwood’s high cliffs above Darkshore.",sec={{t="A Precarious Foothold",b="Bloodvenom Post clings to Felwood’s high cliffs above Darkshore. A narrow trail follows the corrupted southern bank of the Bloodvenom River from the main road. Traditional tauren tents, totems, and watch posts give Horde wanderers a base in the dying forest. Scouts watch demonic forces advancing through the region and study the corruption in the waters. They also track wildlife changed by the Burning Legion’s lingering power.",sp=0},{t="Eyes Across the Ridge",b="From the cliffs, Bloodvenom Post overlooks Felwood’s tainted wilds and northern Darkshore. Its remote position lets Horde forces watch night elf movements along the western coast. The camp also lies well beyond easy reach of Alliance patrols on the forest’s central road.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Bloodvenom Post located?",a="Bloodvenom Post clings to the western ridges of central Felwood. From the main north-south road, follow a narrow trail west along the rocky hillside beside the southern bank of the Bloodvenom River.",al={"find bloodvenom post","how to get to bloodvenom post","bloodvenom post directions"}},{q="Who controls this outpost?",a="Tauren guards hold Bloodvenom Post for the Horde. Its buildings follow traditional tauren designs.",al={"who runs bloodvenom post","bloodvenom post faction"}},{q="Why is the post named Bloodvenom?",a="Bloodvenom Post takes its name from the nearby Bloodvenom River. Demonic corruption has fouled its waters and made them toxic.",al={"why bloodvenom","bloodvenom name meaning"}},{q="What threats do the scouts face here?",a="Scouts face Felwood’s corrupted wildlife, including rabid sabers, tainted oozes, and twisted treants. The Shadow Council and remnants of the Burning Legion also haunt the zone.",al={"bloodvenom enemies","what attacks bloodvenom post"}}},ang={["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you can find shelter and a base at this camp in Felwood’s hostile wilderness. It is the Horde’s only fortified refuge in the zone.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you join the braves who maintain this post. You study the Legion’s damage to the land and fight the corruption harming its natural spirits."},kw={"bloodvenom post","bloodvenom river","darkshore cliffs","felwood","horde outpost","tauren"},rel={"subzone:bloodvenom-river","zone:felwood","topic:tauren","topic:horde","zone:darkshore"},src={"Bloodvenom Post"}}
E["subzone:bloodvenom-river"] = {t="subzone",n="Bloodvenom River",z="felwood",s="In central Felwood, Bloodvenom River bears the forest’s demonic corruption downstream. Its waters cross the mountains into Darkshore and continue as the tainted Wildbend River.",h="In central Felwood, Bloodvenom River bears the forest’s demonic corruption downstream.",sec={{t="A Vein of Corruption",b="Bloodvenom River cuts through Felwood’s corrupted heart, carrying the forest’s decay. Vile oozes, mutated beasts, and foul runoff line its banks, left by the Burning Legion’s invasion. The corruption flows west through the mountains into Darkshore. There, the river continues as the Wildbend River.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the river corrupted?",a="Bloodvenom River runs through central Felwood, an ancient night elven forest warped by the Burning Legion’s demonic magic during the Third War. The corruption soaked into the land and water, leaving noxious sludge and necrotic ooze in the river.",al={"bloodvenom river taint","why is the water green","felwood river poison"}},{q="Where does the Bloodvenom River flow?",a="Bloodvenom River flows through Felwood’s tainted valley, then spills through the mountains into Darkshore. Beyond the ridge, its corrupted waters continue downstream as the Wildbend River.",al={"bloodvenom river path","where does it go","river to darkshore"}},{q="What creatures live along the riverbanks?",a="Noxious oozes, warped wildlife, and corrupted predators live along Bloodvenom River’s waters and muddy banks. The demonic blight draws them there or creates them.",al={"bloodvenom river wildlife","mobs near bloodvenom river","monsters in the river"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see Bloodvenom River carry fel taint across regions. It wounds Kalimdor’s sacred groves and calls for nature’s restoration.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see ancestral woodland waters poison Darkshore through the Wildbend River. It is a bitter reminder of the Legion’s lingering wound."},kw={"bloodvenom river","corruption","darkshore","felwood","ooze","tainted water","wildbend river"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:wildbend-river","zone:darkshore"},src={"Bloodvenom River"}}
E["subzone:deadwood-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Deadwood Village",z="felwood",s="In southern Felwood, Deadwood Village's furbolgs defend their rough wooden homes from all who approach. Once peaceful and close to nature, they fell to the demonic corruption that blighted the forest.",h="In southern Felwood, Deadwood Village's furbolgs defend their rough wooden homes from all who approach.",sec={{t="A Fallen Tribe",b="Near Felwood's southern border, the Deadwood tribe gathers in its village. When demonic energies swept through the ancient woodlands, the furbolgs could not resist the creeping rot. Fel malice warped their minds, and they abandoned their traditions and harmony with nature.\n\nNow brutes, shamans, and den watchers defend their polluted grounds against intruders. Their violence brings despair to their uncorrupted cousins, the Timbermaw.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="Demonic corruption overcame the furbolgs of Deadwood Village when Felwood was blighted during the Third War. Fel magic twisted their natural instincts into rabid aggression, leaving them violently insane and hostile to outsiders.",al={"deadwood hostility","why attack","why are deadwood red"}},{q="Can players talk to or make peace with Deadwood Village?",a="No. The Deadwood tribe is too deeply corrupted for peace. Adventurers hunt them for tribal feathers and to win favor with the uncorrupted Timbermaw furbolgs, who guard the tunnels to the north.",al={"can you be friendly with deadwood","deadwood reputation"}},{q="How does this tribe relate to the Timbermaw?",a="The Deadwood and Timbermaw were once furbolg tribes that lived in harmony with nature. When Felwood was corrupted, the Timbermaw kept their sanity, but the Deadwood fell to fel madness. The Timbermaw now see them as fallen and dangerous.",al={"timbermaw and deadwood","furbolg tribes"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, Deadwood Village shows how deeply demonic corruption can twist peaceful creatures and how nature's defenses can fail."},kw={"corruption","deadwood","deadwood village","felwood","furbolg","timbermaw"},rel={"zone:felwood","topic:furbolg"},src={"Deadwood Village"}}
E["subzone:emerald-sanctuary"] = {t="subzone",n="Emerald Sanctuary",z="felwood",s="At Felwood’s southern entrance, druids gather at Emerald Sanctuary to study the demonic taint and heal the woods.",h="At Felwood’s southern entrance, druids gather at Emerald Sanctuary to study the demonic taint and heal the...",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Blight",b="At Felwood’s southern edge, Emerald Sanctuary is the Cenarion Circle’s base in the blighted woods. Night elven and tauren druids work side by side here, setting aside the factional conflicts spreading across Kalimdor to restore the land. Researchers track corrupted flora and study Jaedenar, seeking a way to cleanse the poisoned soil.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Emerald Sanctuary?",a="The Cenarion Circle established the camp to study and counter the demonic taint choking Felwood. Druids investigate corrupted plants, beasts, and water, then coordinate efforts against Shadow Council cultists deeper in the woods.",al={"why is emerald sanctuary here","what do druids do here","emerald sanctuary purpose"}},{q="Can both Alliance and Horde visit the Emerald Sanctuary?",a="Yes. The Cenarion Circle is independent and neutral. It welcomes visitors from both the Alliance and the Horde who will help cleanse Felwood’s deep corruption.",al={"is emerald sanctuary neutral","horde allowed emerald sanctuary","alliance sanctuary friendly"}},{q="What threat concerns the druids here the most?",a="Druids fear the demonic energies that have warped the whole forest since the Third War, especially at Jaedenar. The sprawling caverns to the north shelter the Shadow Council, which spreads corruption through the woods.",al={"biggest threat in felwood","what are druids fighting","jaedenar threat"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid of Darnassus or Thunder Bluff, you share a mandate to heal the land that reaches beyond faction loyalties."},kw={"cenarion circle","corruption","druids","emerald sanctuary","felwood","jaedenar"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:jaedenar","subzone:talonbranch-glade","subzone:bloodvenom-post","topic:druid"},src={"Emerald Sanctuary"}}
E["subzone:felpaw-village"] = {t="subzone",n="Felpaw Village",z="felwood",s="At Felpaw Village, corrupted furbolgs guard Felwood’s northern path to Timbermaw Hold. Demonic blight has turned the settlement against all outsiders.",h="At Felpaw Village, corrupted furbolgs guard Felwood’s northern path to Timbermaw Hold.",sec={{t="A Stronghold of Corruption",b="Corrupted Deadwood furbolgs hold Felwood’s northern edge at Felpaw Village. Once gentle wardens of the forest, they fell to the demonic blight unleashed during the Third War and became feral. Crude huts and ritual totems fill their blighted enclave. Near the tunnel entrance to Timbermaw Hold, hostile warriors attack anyone who comes close.",sp=0},{t="A Thorn Beside Timbermaw Hold",b="At Felwood’s northern mouth, Timbermaw guards watch over the few uncorrupted furbolgs left in the region. They mourn their fallen cousins, yet keep their guard. The Deadwood threaten the passage to Timbermaw Hold and could carry corruption through its gates into Moonglade and Winterspring. So the guards call on travelers to thin their ranks and seize their ritual fetishes.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who lives in Felpaw Village?",a="Deadwood furbolgs live in Felpaw Village. Demonic corruption spreading across Felwood has overtaken the local tribe.",al={"felpaw village inhabitants","who is at felpaw","deadwood furbolgs northern felwood"}},{q="Why are the furbolgs here hostile?",a="Demonic energies poisoning Felwood’s soil, water, and wildlife drove the Deadwood furbolgs mad. They see outsiders as enemies and cannot be reasoned with.",al={"why do deadwood attack","are felpaw furbolgs friendly","why are bears angry felwood"}},{q="Where is Felpaw Village located?",a="Felpaw Village lies at Felwood’s far northern end, along the road to Timbermaw Hold’s main southern entrance.",al={"felpaw village map location","where is felpaw village","how to get to felpaw"}},{q="How does Felpaw Village relate to Timbermaw Hold?",a="The uncorrupted Timbermaw watch Felpaw Village from their nearby gates. The Deadwood threaten the passage between Felwood, Winterspring, and Moonglade. The Timbermaw reward outsiders who thin the village’s hostile ranks and recover Deadwood ritual feathers.",al={"timbermaw connection","timbermaw hold reputation felpaw","timbermaw deadwood"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid devoted to restoring the natural order, you may see the fallen Deadwood of Felpaw Village as a tragic reminder of the Legion’s lingering poison in sacred forests.",["race:NightElf"]="Night Elves once counted the furbolgs as steadfast allies. For you, the Deadwood’s madness and ritual debasement at Felpaw make that loss especially bitter."},kw={"corruption","deadwood","felpaw","felpaw village","felwood","furbolg","timbermaw"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:timbermaw-hold","topic:furbolg"},src={"Felpaw Village"}}
E["subzone:irontree-woods"] = {t="subzone",n="Irontree Woods",z="felwood",s="Across northern Felwood, Irontree Woods lies blighted by the scars of the Third War. Its ancient protectors stand petrified among twisted treants and elementals.",h="Across northern Felwood, Irontree Woods lies blighted by the scars of the Third War.",sec={{t="A Forest Turned to Stone",b="Irontree Woods lies quiet beneath a demonic stain. During the Third War, the Burning Legion's taint choked life from the soil of this kaldorei glade. The guardian Ancients Hastat, Stoma, and Vartrus fell to dark magic and hardened into stone. Their lifeless forms remain among the corrupted brush.\n\nMaddened treants, vile bog beasts, and tainted water elementals roam the twisted forest floor. They strike at travelers who come near.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What happened to the giant trees here?",a="The great living trees of the night elves, the Ancients Hastat, Stoma, and Vartrus, succumbed to demonic corruption during the Third War. Dark energies turned them to stone, where they remain lifeless.",al={"why are trees stone","petrified ancients","irontree stone trees"}},{q="Why are the creatures in the woods hostile?",a="The Burning Legion's fel corruption has driven the woods' native inhabitants mad. Treants, bog beasts, and water elementals are twisted in mind and form, and attack any outsiders they meet.",al={"angry treants felwood","corrupted elementals irontree"}},{q="Can Irontree Woods ever recover from the corruption?",a="Irontree Woods is deeply warped, and its guardian Ancients are dead and petrified. Hope of recovery rests with the druids working to cleanse the demonic corruption gripping all of Felwood.",al={"healing irontree woods","can felwood be saved","new ancient irontree"}},{q="Who used to care for this grove?",a="The night elves and their allied Ancients once tended and protected this glade. Kaldorei stonework, relics, and petrified guardian trees remain scattered across northern Felwood.",al={"night elf irontree","who built the statues"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="Among the petrified forms of Hastat, Stoma, and Vartrus, you see the toll the Third War took on your sacred woodlands.",["class:Druid"]="Twisted bog beasts and petrified Ancients reveal how far demonic blight has spread. Pure moonwell waters may help renew the tainted soil."},kw={"ancients","felwood","hastat","irontree woods","moonwell","petrified trees","stoma","treants","vartrus"},rel={"zone:felwood","topic:night-elf","topic:burning-legion","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},src={"Irontree Woods"}}
E["subzone:jadefire-run"] = {t="subzone",n="Jadefire Run",z="felwood",s="Jadefire Run shelters Felwood’s strongest and most cunning satyrs in the north. Their fortified camp spreads demonic corruption through the tainted woods.",h="Jadefire Run shelters Felwood’s strongest and most cunning satyrs in the north.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Deceit",b="In northern Felwood, Jadefire satyrs hold a stronghold among the blighted woods. Demonic structures shelter formidable spellcasters and tricksters, far stronger than those in the valley’s lesser outposts. The satyrs use dark sorcery and foul trickery against anyone who enters their territory. They seek to spread corruption farther across Kalimdor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Jadefire Run?",a="Jadefire Run is a major satyr settlement in northern Felwood. It shelters some of the forest’s most dangerous and elite satyrs.",al={"jadefire run info","what is this place felwood"}},{q="Who rules or lives in Jadefire Run?",a="Jadefire Run is home to the Jadefire satyrs, corrupted servants of the Burning Legion. They use fel magic and deceptive illusions to terrorize the surrounding forest.",al={"who lives here","jadefire run mobs"}},{q="Why is Jadefire Run so dangerous?",a="The satyrs of Jadefire Run are stronger and more organized than those in southern Felwood. Their demonic structures and potent spellcasters make them dangerous to the unprepared.",al={"is jadefire run hard","jadefire run danger"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you see Jadefire Run as a reminder of ancient betrayal and demonic defilement on Kalimdor’s sacred soil. It must be cleansed.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you see Jadefire Run’s vile rituals and fel presence as an open wound poisoning Felwood’s natural spirits."},kw={"corrupted","demons","felwood","jadefire","jadefire run","satyr","xavaric"},rel={"zone:felwood","topic:satyr"},src={"Jadefire Run"}}
E["subzone:jaedenar"] = {t="subzone",n="Jaedenar",z="felwood",s="Cultists and demons now hold Jaedenar, the Shadow Council’s chief base in northern Kalimdor. Blighted woodland covers ancient night elf ruins and druidic barrow dens, with the Shadow Hold below.",h="Cultists and demons now hold Jaedenar, the Shadow Council’s chief base in northern Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Bastion of Fel Worship",b="Night elf sacred grounds and barrow dens once filled these hollows. Druids slept in the dens while connected to the Emerald Dream. After the Third War, the Shadow Council claimed the valley and named it for the demon lord Kil'jaeden. Renegade orc and Forsaken warlocks gathered there with satyrs, succubi, and felguards. They hold the surface ruins and deeper barrow dens, turning sacred woodland into a center for demonic rites.",sp=0},{t="The Gates of the Shadow Hold",b="Cultists gather at profane sites above ground, including the Shrine of the Deceiver. Braziers burn with fel flame, and rituals further corrupt the timberland. Below lies the entrance to the Shadow Hold, where the council's true masters direct their work across Felwood. The Emerald Sanctuary watches Jaedenar with concern. It regularly calls on daring wanderers to disrupt summoning circles and douse the dark flames sealing the tunnels.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Jaedenar named after?",a="The Shadow Council named Jaedenar in worship of Kil'jaeden the Deceiver, a supreme commander of the Burning Legion.",al={"jaedenar name origin","why is it called jaedenar","jaedenar namesake"}},{q="Who controls Jaedenar?",a="The Shadow Council controls Jaedenar. Its warlocks, chiefly orcs and Forsaken, serve the Burning Legion alongside summoned demons and corrupted satyrs.",al={"who runs jaedenar","jaedenar faction","enemies in jaedenar"}},{q="What was here before the demons arrived?",a="Before the Third War, ancient night elf ruins and peaceful druidic barrow dens stood here. Druids rested in the dens while roaming the Emerald Dream.",al={"jaedenar history","who lived in jaedenar","jaedenar barrow dens"}},{q="What is the Shadow Hold?",a="The Shadow Hold is a subterranean cavern system beneath Jaedenar and the fortified headquarters of the Shadow Council's leadership in Felwood. Its caverns were once druidic barrow dens.",al={"what is shadow hold","cave in jaedenar","underground jaedenar"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you walk sacred ground laid waste. Jaedenar's barrows were once peaceful sanctuaries where druids communed with the Emerald Dream; now demonic ichor drowns them.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you see the Shadow Council's enduring presence on Azeroth in Jaedenar. Its warlocks openly summon powerful demons and wield volatile fel sorcery."},kw={"barrow dens","deceiver","felwood","jaedenar","kil'jaeden","shadow council","shadow hold"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:shadow-hold","topic:shadow-council","npc:greta-mosshoof","topic:emerald-dream","topic:satyr","topic:forsaken"},src={"Jaedenar"}}
E["subzone:morlos-aran"] = {t="subzone",n="Morlos'Aran",z="felwood",s="In southern Felwood, Morlos'Aran lies in ruins beneath demonic blight. The ancient night elf settlement flourished before the Great Sundering.",h="In southern Felwood, Morlos'Aran lies in ruins beneath demonic blight.",sec={{t="Echoes of the Golden Age",b="Before the Sundering, Morlos'Aran was a grand center of ancient kaldorei life. Like Ameth'Aran, Bashal'Aran, and Ordil'Aran across northern Kalimdor, its marble arches and moonlit plazas held elven life and arcana. The Well of Eternity collapsed, and the city broke apart. Its shattered colonnades remain from the height of kaldorei civilization.",sp=0},{t="A Blighted Relic",b="During the Third War, the Burning Legion trampled the corridor where Morlos'Aran stood. Demonic corruption and toxic mire choked its surviving foundations. The ruins suffered a grimmer fate than those in Darkshore and Ashenvale, where decay and wilderness took hold. Today, wandering beasts, corrupted elementals, and remnants of shadow forces haunt the ruins and linger in Felwood.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Morlos'Aran originally?",a="Morlos'Aran was a major night elf settlement that thrived before the Great Sundering. Along with sister cities across ancient Kalimdor, it belonged to the heart of kaldorei civilization before falling into ruin ten thousand years ago.",al={"what is morlos aran","morlos'aran history","who built morlos aran"}},{q="Why does the name end in ''Aran'?",a="The meaning of the suffix isn't recorded. It appears in several pre-Sundering night elf cities, including Ameth'Aran and Bashal'Aran in Darkshore, Ordil'Aran in Ashenvale, and Tethris'Aran in Desolace.",al={"meaning of aran","aran suffix","ameth aran connection"}},{q="Where exactly is Morlos'Aran located?",a="Morlos'Aran lies in southern Felwood, near the border crossing from Ashenvale. Its crumbling marble architecture can be seen among the corrupted, withered trees just off the main path.",al={"morlos aran location","where is morlos'aran","finding morlos aran"}},{q="What threats wander these ruins today?",a="Corrupted wildlife, tainted treants, and lingering demonic spawn infest the forest around Morlos'Aran. They make the ruins extremely hazardous for travelers heading north into Felwood.",al={"what is inside morlos'aran","morlos aran mobs","dangers of morlos aran"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Morlos'Aran offers a tragic reminder of how far the empire fell. Sacred ancestral stonework now lies swallowed by the Legion's foul demonic corruption.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you can see the damage to Felwood in the twisted earth around Morlos'Aran's foundations. The ruin spurs Cenarion efforts to purify the land."},kw={"ameth'aran","bashal'aran","felwood","kaldorei","morlos aran","morlos'aran","ruins","sundering"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:ameth-aran","quest:954","zone:ashenvale","zone:darkshore","zone:desolace","topic:night-elf"},src={"Morlos'Aran"}}
E["subzone:ruins-of-constellas"] = {t="subzone",n="Ruins of Constellas",z="felwood",s="At Mount Hyjal’s roots, Jadefire satyrs hold the Ruins of Constellas in Felwood. Their fel magic has corrupted the settlement’s moonwell.",h="At Mount Hyjal’s roots, Jadefire satyrs hold the Ruins of Constellas in Felwood.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Broken arches and crumbling plazas mark the night elf settlement that once stood at Constellas. The Burning Legion marched through Felwood during the Third War and shattered the haven. Demonic corruption followed. Now Jadefire satyrs hold the ruins.\n\nXavathras leads the satyrs as they tend the defiled moonwell. They turn its pure waters into fel power for their master, Lord Xavaric.",sp=0},{t="The Struggle for Cleansing",b="Those who work to cleanse Felwood face a foul corruption at Constellas. Xavathras and his Jadefire satyrs guard their tents among the ruins. At the heart of the settlement lies the tainted moonwell. The satyrs fight to keep their work safe from anyone who would end it.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What was Constellas before the corruption?",a="Constellas was an ancient night elf settlement near Mount Hyjal’s base. Its architecture and moonwell suggest a serene grove devoted to Elune and nature before the Burning Legion invaded Felwood during the Third War.",al={"constellas history","what was constellas","who built constellas"}},{q="Who controls the ruins now?",a="Jadefire satyrs occupy the ruins, led by Xavathras. They cultivate demonic energies throughout the area under Lord Xavaric’s command.",al={"who lives here","who rules constellas","jadefire satyrs constellas"}},{q="What happened to the moonwell in Constellas?",a="Jadefire satyrs seized the moonwell and corrupted it with fel magic. Xavathras tends it as a toxic source of fel energy instead of a wellspring of Elune’s soothing blessings.",al={"corrupted moonwell felwood","constellas moonwell","why is the well green"}},{q="Who is Xavaric?",a="Xavaric is a cruel Jadefire satyr served by Xavathras. The satyrs tend Constellas’s corrupted moonwell on Xavaric’s behalf.",al={"xavaric","who does xavathras serve"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you may see Constellas’s desecration and its corrupted moonwell as an affront to Elune. Driving out the Jadefire satyrs would restore what they defiled.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you may see Constellas’s defiled moonwell as a reminder of your vow to restore balance to Felwood."},kw={"constellas","felwood","jadefire","moonwell","satyr","xavaric","xavathras"},rel={"zone:felwood","npc:xavathras","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf","topic:druid","subzone:moonwell-ashenvale"},src={"Ruins of Constellas"}}
E["subzone:shadow-hold"] = {t="subzone",n="Shadow Hold",z="felwood",s="In the depths of Jaedenar, the Shadow Council holds Shadow Hold as its chief stronghold on Kalimdor. The cult rules from a defiled night elf barrow den beneath Felwood's blighted canyon.",h="In the depths of Jaedenar, the Shadow Council holds Shadow Hold as its chief stronghold on Kalimdor.",sec={{t="A Defiled Sanctuary",b="Beneath Jaedenar's corrupted red earth, Shadow Hold's corridors wind through an ancient night elf barrow den. Druids once slept here while tending the Emerald Dream. Now warlocks and demonic servants stalk its twisted passages by fel fire. Lord Banehollow, Prince Xavalis, and Shadow Lord Fel'dan command a formidable force in the deepest tiers. From here, demonic power holds its chief seat in the region.",sp=0},{t="Horrors in the Deep",b="The Shadow Council directs its corruption of Felwood from the caverns and tortures its prisoners. Among those taken deep inside were Arko'narin Starshade, a night elf, and Trey Lightforge, a human paladin.\n\nArko'narin survived after a timely rescue, but the cult tortured Trey to death. His spirit was briefly twisted to malice before he was laid to rest. The Emerald Circle and local shamans still work to pierce the dark barriers around the hold and strike down its demonic masters.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What was Shadow Hold before the Shadow Council took it over?",a="Before the Shadow Council seized Shadow Hold, it was an ancient night elf barrow den. Druids slept there as they tended the land and their communion with the Emerald Dream. After the Third War and Felwood's demonic corruption, the cult took the complex and defiled its sacred halls into a fel fortress.",al={"shadow hold history","who built shadow hold","what was shadow hold originally"}},{q="Who rules inside Shadow Hold?",a="Lord Banehollow oversees Shadow Hold with his lieutenants, the satyr Prince Xavalis and the warlock Shadow Lord Fel'dan. Fel'dan commands the mortal cultists.",al={"shadow hold boss","who is in charge of shadow hold","leaders of shadow hold"}},{q="Why would an adventurer infiltrate Shadow Hold peacefully?",a="Those who practice the dark arts may enter Shadow Hold disguised as loyal cultists to seek summoning reagents such as Xorothian Stardust. Lord Banehollow permits trade with outsiders only after they prove their loyalty by rooting out spies and traitors among his ranks.",al={"infiltrate shadow hold","shadow council disguise shadow hold","xorothian stardust shadow hold"},sp=1},{q="What happened to the captives in the hold?",a="The Shadow Council captured Arko'narin Starshade, a night elf, and Trey Lightforge, a paladin, while they scouted the cult. The cultist Rakaiah tortured Trey to death. Adventurers rescued Arko'narin from her cage and later recovered Trey's remains for a proper burial.",al={"jaedenar prisoners","trey lightforge and arkonarin","shadow hold cage"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you can seek rare demonic reagents such as Xorothian Stardust in Shadow Hold's deepest recesses. Lord Banehollow grants access only to those who win his favor through cunning infiltration.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you find an ancestral barrow den defiled by fel sludge and demonic rituals. Imprisonment cages fill the hold."},kw={"arko'narin","banehollow","barrow den","fel'dan","felwood","jaedenar","shadow council","shadow hold","trey lightforge"},rel={"subzone:jaedenar","zone:felwood","topic:shadow-council","npc:greta-mosshoof","npc:islen-waterseer","topic:satyr","topic:night-elf"},src={"Shadow Hold"}}
E["subzone:shatter-scar-vale"] = {t="subzone",n="Shatter Scar Vale",z="felwood",s="Fel fire still burns in Shatter Scar Vale, north of Bloodvenom Falls in central Felwood. The vale bears the marks of the infernals that struck northern Kalimdor during the Third War, and demons remain among the craters.",h="Fel fire still burns in Shatter Scar Vale, north of Bloodvenom Falls in central Felwood.",sec={{t="Impact of the Infernals",b="During the Third War, the Burning Legion sent living siege engines against northern Kalimdor. Shatter Scar Vale bore the force of that assault. Demonic infernals fell from the sky, breaking through the ancient canopy and striking deep into the earth. Their blows shattered the ground and left blackened hollows that still smolder with unholy fire.\n\nThe Legion was broken at Mount Hyjal, but the infernals and lesser demons did not disperse. They remain entrenched in the scarred earth.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is the ground covered in craters?",a="The craters were made by infernals the Burning Legion sent against the forest during the Third War. These hulking constructs of fel stone fell from the sky and struck the ground, leaving scars that still smolder across the vale.",al={"craters in felwood","why is shatter scar vale cratered","what made the craters"}},{q="What creatures roam Shatter Scar Vale?",a="Constructs and servants of the Burning Legion still roam the vale. Living infernals guard the smoldering impact basins, with lesser demons left behind when the invasion faltered.",al={"what mobs are here","shatter scar vale enemies"}},{q="Where is Shatter Scar Vale located?",a="Shatter Scar Vale lies in central Felwood, directly north of Bloodvenom Falls along the eastern side of the forest's main path.",al={"shatter scar vale location","where is shatter scar vale"}}},ang={["class:Warlock"]="The fel-infused cores of the infernals in these craters hold chaotic magic left by the Legion's invasion.",["class:Druid"]="The smoldering scars in this vale remain open wounds in Kalimdor's spirit. They refuse to heal while the Legion's constructs still burn."},kw={"bloodvenom falls","burning legion","craters","felwood","infernals","shatter scar vale"},rel={"zone:felwood","topic:burning-legion","subzone:bloodvenom-falls","topic:third-war"},src={"Shatter Scar Vale"}}
E["subzone:talonbranch-glade"] = {t="subzone",n="Talonbranch Glade",z="felwood",s="Night elves find a rare refuge at Talonbranch Glade in northern Felwood. South of Timbermaw Hold, the glade offers a moonwell, shelter, and hippogryph flights amid the blighted woods.",h="Night elves find a rare refuge at Talonbranch Glade in northern Felwood.",sec={{t="A Beacon in the Blight",b="Talonbranch Glade watches over the high ground near the tunnel to Timbermaw Hold. It is the Alliance’s northernmost bastion in Felwood, gathered around a sheltered night elf lodge and a working moonwell. Scouts, Sentinels, and travelers rest here before venturing deeper into the tainted woods or setting out for Winterspring and Moonglade.",sp=0},{t="A Crossroads of the North",b="Hippogryphs carry travelers from Talonbranch Glade to Auberdine in Darkshore and Everlook beyond Timbermaw Hold. The outpost keeps watch against the Shadow Council’s encroaching shadows and the feral beast packs roaming the corrupted vales.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is Talonbranch Glade?",a="Talonbranch Glade is an Alliance encampment in northern Felwood. Sentinels, druids, and travelers find refuge and rest there among the corrupted forest.",al={"talonbranch","talonbranch purpose","what is this place"}},{q="Where does the flight master here fly to?",a="The hippogryphs at Talonbranch Glade fly to Auberdine, Everlook, and Moonglade.",al={"talonbranch flight paths","flight points","where can i fly"}},{q="Is the water in the moonwell safe to drink?",a="Yes. Elune still blesses the moonwell at Talonbranch Glade, and demonic corruption has not touched it. Felwood’s pools and springs are tainted.",al={"talonbranch moonwell","is the water clean","moonwell corrupted"}},{q="How close is this to Timbermaw Hold?",a="Talonbranch Glade lies directly south of the entrance to Timbermaw Hold. It offers a final resting place before the furbolg tunnels lead into Winterspring or Moonglade.",al={"where is timbermaw hold","path to winterspring"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can find your northernmost working outpost in Felwood at Talonbranch Glade. It offers flight connections, repairs, and sanctuary near Timbermaw Hold.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can find an untouched moonwell at Talonbranch Glade. It is a sign of Elune’s enduring grace amid the demonic blight choking the ancient forest."},kw={"felwood","flight point","glade","moonwell","sentinels","talonbranch","timbermaw"},rel={"zone:felwood","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:emerald-sanctuary","subzone:everlook","subzone:auberdine","topic:alliance","topic:elune"},src={"Talonbranch Glade"}}
E["zone:felwood"] = {t="zone",n="Felwood",z="felwood",s="Felwood remains in the grip of corruption between Ashenvale and Mount Hyjal. Once a paradise tended by night elves, it was poisoned by demonic magic during the Third War. Satyrs, twisted beasts, and ancients roam its depths as the Cenarion Circle and Alliance and Horde outposts work to cleanse it.",h="Felwood remains in the grip of corruption between Ashenvale and Mount Hyjal.",sec={{t="A Paradise Befouled",b="Before the Third War, clear streams ran beneath singing birds, and ancient protectors guarded the peaceful groves. Then the dreadlord Tichondrius and the Burning Legion brought that peace to an end. Before their assault on Mount Hyjal, they used the Skull of Gul'dan to poison northern Kalimdor. Its sorcery blackened the forest floor and turned it to mire.\n\nIllidan Stormrage later slew Tichondrius and consumed the artifact's essence. Yet the fel corruption remained. Treants and ancients rotted within, rivers boiled with bile, and the forest's beasts fell into cannibalistic madness.",sp=0},{t="The War for Cleansing",b="The work of healing Felwood is slow. On its southern border, the Cenarion Circle fights the blight from the Emerald Sanctuary. Its druids tend poisoned songflowers and night dragon bulbs, and give wanderers Cenarion beacons and cleansing salves.\n\nThe night elves hold Talonbranch Glade in the north, while the Horde keeps Bloodvenom Post. Both footholds stand amid a deadly wilderness where nature has turned against mortal flesh.",sp=0},{t="The Shadow in Jaedenar",b="Cultists still nurture Felwood's fel taint. In the underground labyrinth of Jaedenar and Shadow Hold, remnants of the Shadow Council perform foul rituals under Lord Banehollow's direction. They are allied with deceitful satyrs who desecrate ancient moonwells.\n\nThe warlocks draw upon the forest's agony and summon demonic reinforcements. Felwood cannot be redeemed while the council remains rooted here.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is Felwood corrupted?",a="During the Third War, the dreadlord Tichondrius used the demonic Skull of Gul'dan to corrupt the forest. The Legion sought to weaken the night elves' defenses before its march on Mount Hyjal. Wildlife, water, and ancients were blighted.",al={"how did felwood get corrupted","what happened to felwood","why are the trees dead"}},{q="Can the corrupted plants in the forest be cleansed?",a="Yes. Druids of the Cenarion Circle provide salves brewed from collected fel taints and mineral residues. Apply them to songflowers, whiplash tubers, and night dragons to purge their corruption and gain restorative fruit and blessings.",al={"how to cleanse plants","cenarion plant salve","corrupted songflower"}},{q="Who controls Jaedenar?",a="The clandestine Shadow Council, a sect of mortal warlocks and demon worshippers, controls Jaedenar. From the underground caverns of Shadow Hold, the dreadlord Lord Banehollow oversees their rituals and commands the satyrs in the region.",al={"what is jaedenar","who is in shadow hold","jaedenar boss"}},{q="Are the furbolgs in Felwood hostile?",a="Most are hostile. The Deadwood tribes have wholly succumbed to demonic corruption and fel madness. The Timbermaw hold the northern tunnel network and remain uncorrupted, but distrust outsiders until they prove friendly.",al={"felwood furbolgs","timbermaw furbolgs","deadwood village"}},{q="How do you get to Moonglade or Winterspring through Felwood?",a="The road north leads into Timbermaw Hold, a fortified cavern complex. The uncorrupted Timbermaw furbolgs control the tunnels from Felwood to Moonglade and Winterspring. You must earn their trust or fight your way through.",al={"timbermaw tunnel","road to winterspring","pass to moonglade"}},{q="Why do the corrupted ancients attack night elves?",a="Demonic magic warped and poisoned the once-noble ancients and treants. Eternal agony has shattered their minds, and they resent the night elves, whom they believe abandoned them to the Burning Legion.",al={"mad treants","corrupted ancients","why ancients hostile"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For the Cenarion Circle, Felwood is a profound tragedy. As a druid, you dedicate your life to cleansing its blighted plants and calming maddened nature spirits.",["race:NightElf"]="As a kaldorei, you know the desecration of these ancient woods brings immense grief and shame. Your people failed to protect them from the Legion's touch.",["class:Warlock"]="As a warlock, you find Felwood's dark tunnels and lingering demonic forces a focal point in your hunt for rival Shadow Council cultists.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you can gather rare, volatile flora from Felwood's fel-soaked earth. Few places in Azeroth offer Gromsblood and Arthas' Tears."},kw={"banehollow","bloodvenom","deadwood","emerald sanctuary","felwood","jaedenar","songflower","talonbranch","tichondrius","timbermaw"},rel={"subzone:emerald-sanctuary","subzone:jaedenar","subzone:timbermaw-hold","subzone:talonbranch-glade","subzone:bloodvenom-post","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:shadow-council","zone:ashenvale"},src={"Felwood (Classic)","Felwood"}}
